cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  correlation-threshold-selection: replication package for a benchmark of
  correlation-threshold feature selection in penalised regression
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software and
  the paper it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdullah
    family-names: Hamad
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullah-shekha/correlation-threshold-selection"
abstract: >-
  A controlled benchmark of correlation-threshold feature selection in penalised
  regression over 24 public datasets, 9 selection arms and 5 estimators, under
  nested repeated cross-validation. No pruning arm improved predictive accuracy
  on any estimator, and harm rose steadily as the threshold tightened. A paired
  permutation study shows that where the rule acts its output is not determined
  by the data alone: permuting the input columns moves test error by a median of
  3.46%, and chance-corrected selection stability across permutations is 0.479
  against 0.981 for an order-invariant control. The package contains the
  implementation, the dataset manifest, all 80,100 fold-level results, and a
  verification script that re-derives every table in the paper from them.
keywords:
  - multicollinearity
  - feature selection
  - penalised regression
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark
  - variance inflation factor
